{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ExZ6nMVQRRmfw1HfDjMUF","type":"tool_result","content":"30\t   ``project_dir()`` is ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` (the harness-set project\n31\t   root) when present, else ``os.getcwd()``.\n32\t\n33\t## Slug-family archaeology (measured S319, do not \"fix\")\n34\t\n35\t``~/.claude/projects/`` holds THREE spellings grown by different\n36\teras/agents:\n37\t\n38\t- ``--Users-<user>`` (double leading dash): legacy harness derivation\n39\t  (``'-' + path.replace('/', '-')``). Frozen legacy trees; never\n40\t  written by this module.\n41\t- ``-Users-<user>`` (single leading dash): CURRENT harness derivation and\n42\t  the ADR-001 normative form. This module emits ONLY this spelling.\n43\t- ``ceo-orchestration`` (bare literal): the four-month defect this\n44\t  module cures (587-file family, PLAN-182 W0). Reachable read-only via\n45\t  :func:`legacy_state_dir` for migration/W2 custody tooling ONLY.\n46\t\n47\t## Symlink honesty\n48\t\n49\t``project_dir()`` absolutizes (``os.path.abspath``) but does NOT\n50\t``realpath()``: the harness slugs the launch path as given, and native\n51\talignment (co-location with harness memory) wins over symlink\n52\tcanonicalization. Two spellings of one repo via symlinks therefore get\n53\ttwo state dirs — same behavior the harness itself has for its memory\n54\tdirs. Documented limitation, pinned by test.\n55\t\n56\t## CLI contract (PLAN-182 OQ-6 — Owner decision 2026-08-22, landed S326)\n57\t\n58\tShell consumers get the SAME resolver, never a rebuilt literal::\n59\t\n60\t    python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py [--state-dir | --slug |\n61\t                                                 --project-dir] [--project PATH]\n62\t\n63\t- ``--state-dir`` (default): :func:`runtime_state_dir`; ``--slug``:\n64\t  :func:`project_slug`; ``--project-dir``: the slug input.\n65\t- ``--project PATH`` replaces the slug INPUT (``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` / cwd).\n66\t  ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE`` still wins for ``--state-dir`` — it is the\n67\t  documented operator override, not a default.\n68\t- Read-only: prints ONE path + newline on stdout, creates nothing, exit 0.\n69\t  Usage error: exit 2, message on stderr, NOTHING on stdout (a caller doing\n70\t  ``dir=\"$(...)\"`` must never capture prose as a path).\n71\t- ONE invocation convention. An inline ``python3 -c`` in a template would\n72\t  be a second one, and the class this cures is \"a local branch that\n73\t  re-derives the path\" (CLAUDE.md §4). Consumers: the two pre-push review\n74\t  gates in ``templates/{codex,grok}/``, ``ceo-backup.sh``, ``ceo-restore.sh``.\n75\t\n76\tLeaf module: stdlib only, imports nothing from ``_lib`` (loadable from\n77\tany hook, mirrors ``injection_salt``'s constraint). Python ≥ 3.9.\n78\t\"\"\"\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"554a7565-eb62-4598-9760-aeebd94af377","uuid":"1383483f-b583-4af2-8e4f-59f3f72ddb86","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:41:59.689Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py","content":"   ``project_dir()`` is ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` (the harness-set project\n   root) when present, else ``os.getcwd()``.\n\n## Slug-family archaeology (measured S319, do not \"fix\")\n\n``~/.claude/projects/`` holds THREE spellings grown by different\neras/agents:\n\n- ``--Users-<user>`` (double leading dash): legacy harness derivation\n  (``'-' + path.replace('/', '-')``). Frozen legacy trees; never\n  written by this module.\n- ``-Users-<user>`` (single leading dash): CURRENT harness derivation and\n  the ADR-001 normative form. This module emits ONLY this spelling.\n- ``ceo-orchestration`` (bare literal): the four-month defect this\n  module cures (587-file family, PLAN-182 W0). Reachable read-only via\n  :func:`legacy_state_dir` for migration/W2 custody tooling ONLY.\n\n## Symlink honesty\n\n``project_dir()`` absolutizes (``os.path.abspath``) but does NOT\n``realpath()``: the harness slugs the launch path as given, and native\nalignment (co-location with harness memory) wins over symlink\ncanonicalization. Two spellings of one repo via symlinks therefore get\ntwo state dirs — same behavior the harness itself has for its memory\ndirs. Documented limitation, pinned by test.\n\n## CLI contract (PLAN-182 OQ-6 — Owner decision 2026-08-22, landed S326)\n\nShell consumers get the SAME resolver, never a rebuilt literal::\n\n    python3 .claude/hooks/_lib/runtime_paths.py [--state-dir | --slug |\n                                                 --project-dir] [--project PATH]\n\n- ``--state-dir`` (default): :func:`runtime_state_dir`; ``--slug``:\n  :func:`project_slug`; ``--project-dir``: the slug input.\n- ``--project PATH`` replaces the slug INPUT (``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` / cwd).\n  ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE`` still wins for ``--state-dir`` — it is the\n  documented operator override, not a default.\n- Read-only: prints ONE path + newline on stdout, creates nothing, exit 0.\n  Usage error: exit 2, message on stderr, NOTHING on stdout (a caller doing\n  ``dir=\"$(...)\"`` must never capture prose as a path).\n- ONE invocation convention. An inline ``python3 -c`` in a template would\n  be a second one, and the class this cures is \"a local branch that\n  re-derives the path\" (CLAUDE.md §4). Consumers: the two pre-push review\n  gates in ``templates/{codex,grok}/``, ``ceo-backup.sh``, ``ceo-restore.sh``.\n\nLeaf module: stdlib only, imports nothing from ``_lib`` (loadable from\nany hook, mirrors ``injection_salt``'s constraint). Python ≥ 3.9.\n\"\"\"\n","numLines":50,"startLine":30,"totalLines":277}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016ExZ6nMVQRRmfw1HfDjMUF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
